    tafseerEn: `📖 When Prophet Moses brought down the sacred stone tablets of the Torah filled with Allah's good rules, the people felt lazy. They made excuses: "These rules are too hard! We don't know if we can follow them." So Allah showed them an unforgettable miracle of His power!

Let us learn the clear, word-by-word meaning using simple and friendly words:

- وَرَفَعْنَا فَوْقَكُمُ الطُّورَ (And We raised the Mount high above you):
By Allah's mighty command, the huge, rocky mountain of Sinai was lifted off the earth and suspended right above their heads like a gigantic dark umbrella!
The people were terrified. They dropped to the ground in prostration, with one cheek on the soil and one eye nervously looking up at the floating mountain, fearing it might tumble on them.

- خُذُوا مَا آتَيْنَاكُم بِقُوَّةٍ (Hold firmly to what We gave you with strength):
Following Allah's rules is not a half-hearted game. You cannot say: "I will only obey when I feel like it." Allah told them to hold onto the holy guidance with courage, energy, and strong dedication.

- وَاذْكُرُوا مَا فِيهِ (And remember what is inside it):
Read the good book, memorize its beautiful wisdom, and practice its lessons every day in your speech, kindness, and prayers.

[QUESTION: What miracle did Allah show them over Mount Sinai? | ANSWER: Allah lifted the huge mountain into the air above their heads like a giant hovering canopy!]

[QUESTION: What does "Hold it with strength" mean for us today? | ANSWER: It means practicing our prayers and good deeds with energy, enthusiasm, and focus, without feeling lazy!]

✨ Life's Vital Takeaway: When the Adhan calls for prayer, do not delay or drag your feet! Stand up cheerfully, make fresh Wudu, and pray with focus. Strong believers do good things with energy and joy!`
